 "script": [
  {"id": "hook", "text": "A super typhoon with one hundred ninety-five kilometer winds nears Luzon. Will it make landfall?"},
  {"id": "f1", "text": "PAGASA says Champi entered the Philippine area Tuesday and is now called Rosal. At five p.m., sustained winds were one hundred ninety-five kilometers per hour, with gusts up to two hundred forty. It was about twelve hundred seventy kilometers east of central Luzon."},
  {"id": "f2", "text": "PAGASA raised Signal Number One over Batanes and parts of Cagayan, Isabela and Catanduanes. Higher signals may follow as the storm approaches. The agency says Rosal should not make direct landfall in Batanes, but the northernmost islands may still be affected."},
  {"id": "f3", "text": "For Thursday and Friday, PAGASA forecasts heavy to intense rain of one hundred to two hundred millimeters in Batanes, and waves up to four and a half meters. PAGASA expects weakening to begin Thursday. The closest approach is expected around Friday."},
  {"id": "cta", "text": "Will Rosal stay off the Philippine coast? Yes or no?"}
